{
    "id": 146,
    "title": "Design Release 1: the shared tokens and the app shell",
    "why": "Jason's platform-wide directive (design/css-theme-brand.md §3–4, Release 1; brand.md §4's note, 2026-11-18). (1) ONE SET OF TOKENS for every page, in app/ui/theme-tokens.php, drawn once in each page's head by tv_page_start: brand.md's own values (vellum #EFE3C8, Deep Umber #3E2B1F, Slate-Umbra #231D17, cards #E6D8B5 to #D8C79D, Warm Near-Black #2A1D14, Muted Taupe #7A6A52, copper, sage, amethyst, the cartographic colours), System Red #a62b2b and Grounded Amber #8f5600, type, 150ms ease-out, corners, warm shadows, the gap between groups, focus rings. Lines and metadata text are mixed from brand values (brand.md names none; taupe alone is 4.11:1 on the vellum). (2) THE FONTS served from our own server (website/fonts/, SIL Open Font License): Inter for text on every page now; Merriweather and Playfair Display for headings, moved page by page in Release 3. No visitor is sent to a font company, and the card pages' content policy already allows them. (3) THE APP SHELL (the rail, the workspace heading, crumbs, the phone menu) on the tokens, with no colour of its own: the rail's small labels go from 2.97:1 to 7.4:1, the old Brass Amber (superseded in brand.md) goes, motion is 150ms ease-out, focus rings are sage on the rail. FAQ: one entry on the fonts.",
